.SH "NAME"
pcre2_set_bsr \- set \(rsR convention
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.nf
.fam C
#include <pcre2.h>

int pcre2_set_bsr(pcre2_compile_context *ccontext, uint32_t value);
.fam
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
This function sets the convention for processing \(rsR within a compile context.
The second argument must be one of PCRE2_BSR_ANYCRLF or PCRE2_BSR_UNICODE. The
result is zero for success or PCRE2_ERROR_BADDATA if the second argument is
invalid.
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the POSIX API in the
\f(CRpcre2posix\fP
page.